    }
    #tsIjsmSHV4YNtgJygHtghbEp ^"Craft" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Ability"
        PARAMETERS {
            ^"type"
            OF STRING
        }
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ability Type" STRING "General" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Core Rules"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A general term for countless Abilities, all dealing with handiwork of some type. In general, Craft Abilities are distinguished by the material they work with, although you may also take a Craft Ability that allows the character to work with several materials in one specific way. You may purchase Craft more than once, choosing a different one each time. Skill in one Craft does not imply skill in any others. City and Guild contains more detailed information about Craft Abilities and their use, in Chapter 4. Specialties : as appropriate to the craft."
    }
    #t1PUskgg9A3nDJqnU9igxJYF ^"Profession" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Ability"
        PARAMETERS {
            ^"type"
            OF STRING
        }
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ability Type" STRING "General" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Core Rules"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The ability to do a job which does not involve making something. Examples include jongleur, marshal, reeve, sailor, steward, teamster, and washerwoman. Specialties depend on the profession."
    }
    #tpVjwIM28qoc7jZdFaYRQ39i ^"Living Language" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Ability"
        PARAMETERS {
            ^"language"
            OF STRING
        }
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ability Type" STRING "General" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Core Rules"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Fluency in a particular living language. Rather than a die roll modifier, your score in this Knowledge measures your ability to communicate. When two people speak to each other, the lower Ability score determines how well they communicate. Characters who speak related languages can communicate at a penalty to their scores (assigned by SCORE FLUENCY 0 Point and grunt. With one or more experience points, you know 'please', 'thank you', and a few other words. Basic questions and answers: 'Where is the church?', 'Do you sell food?'. Constant mistakes, and an atrocious accent. People must speak slowly and often repeat themselves, and you cannot string a conversation together. 1 2 Basic conversation. You can sustain a short conversation on a common topic. You still make many mistakes, and often"
    }
    #tAEXILgaQw5Vk2GUp9iAjQo6 ^"Dead Language" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Ability"
        PARAMETERS {
            ^"language"
            OF STRING
        }
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ability Type" STRING "Academic" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Core Rules"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This skill is similar to all other (Language) Abilities, but it is only available to educated characters. It grants the ability to speak a language which is no longer used as a native language in the areas the character has lived in. The most important example is Latin, the language of formal education in the West. It is also the common language of the Church and Order of Hermes. In other areas of the world, Arabic, Greek and Hebrew fill similar functions, although of these only Hebrew is a dead language."
    }
    #tcB2h14VQ7pxqVTU9Q5EPzkF ^"Area Lore" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Ability"
        PARAMETERS {
            ^"area"
            OF STRING
        }
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ability Type" STRING "General" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Core Rules"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Knowledge of one particular region, covenant, or even a village. It includes knowing where things are in the immediate area, local history and legends, and the centers of power in the region. The smaller the region, the more detailed your knowledge."
    }
    #tmLCqaou1tqN1pDLIDgpWM5N ^"Organization Lore" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Ability"
        PARAMETERS {
            ^"organization"
            OF STRING
        }
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Ability Type" STRING "General" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Core Rules"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Knowledge of the legends, history, structure, operation, and goals of the specified organization. Organizations can be as large as the Church, or as small as a local craft guild. The smaller the organization, the more detailed your knowledge. Order of Hermes Lore is particularly important to most magi."
    }
    #t7hNlgBCk78Bdy5eu3OEaWsE ^"Gabriel, the Archangel of Prophecy" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Creature"
        PROPERTIES {
