        ABILITIES {
            "Artes Liberales" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "logic"
            "Awareness" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "when working"
            "Charm" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "equals"
            "Concentration" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "spell casting"
            "Folk Ken" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "magi"
            "Latin" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "Hermetic technical terms"
            "Magic Lore" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "nonHermetic magic"
            "Magic Theory" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "Creo"
            "Native Language" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "educated talk"
            "Order of Hermes Lore" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "great discoveries"
            "Parma Magica" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "Mentem"
            "Penetration" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "Auram"
            "Teaching" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "Hermetic Arts"
        }
        SPELLS_KNOWN {
            ^"Charge of the Angry Winds" TECHNIQUE "Creo" FORM "Auram" LEVEL 15 CASTING_TOTAL 24
            ^"Clouds of Rain and Thunder" TECHNIQUE "Creo" FORM "Auram" LEVEL 25 CASTING_TOTAL 24
            ^"Clouds of Summer Snow" TECHNIQUE "Creo" FORM "Auram" LEVEL 25 CASTING_TOTAL 24
            ^"The Incantation of Lightning" TECHNIQUE "Creo" FORM "Auram" LEVEL 35 CASTING_TOTAL 24
            ^"Purification of the Festering Wounds" TECHNIQUE "Creo" FORM "Corpus" LEVEL 20 CASTING_TOTAL 16
        }
        CHOICES {
            "The Bonisagus is most likely Driven to make some great discovery in magic. He or she is a so-called 'lab rat', a magus happier in his laboratory than in the outside world. However, the favors he owes and his drive to discover are likely to push him out. Similarly, enchanted items are very useful to him, but he is bad at making them for himself. That also tends to drive him into stories. This concept is built around the Virtues and the Driven Flaw; the other Flaws can be changed easily. He can also take two additional Minor Flaws, or make Driven Major, and take two additional Minor Virtues to balance them. Similarly, the Arts in which the character has an Affinity can be changed, but that also requires changing the spells he knows."
        }
    }
