    #t83cde099ef1fa533410ef0 ^"The Champagne Cycle" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Table Columns" LIST ["Fair", "Dates"]
            ^"Source" STRING "City & Guild"
        }
        TABLE {
            "Lagny"
            "January 1 for 6 weeks"
            "Bar-sur-Aube"
            "mid-Lent for 2 weeks"
            "Provins"
            "Ascension week for 6 weeks"
            "Troyes"
            "June 24 for 6 weeks"
            "Provins"
            "September 14 for 6 weeks"
            "Troyes"
            "November 2 for 6 weeks Generally there is an interval of about two weeks in between fairs.

Unlike other fairs, where everything on sale is available throughout the fair, the Champagne fairs regulate trade during the six-week fairs as follows: 1 week for setting up stalls, then ten days for cloth trading, 11 days for leather trading, and 19 days for trade in other goods, followed by a few days for settling accounts."
        }
    }
