            ^"Repeatable" BOOLEAN false
            ^"Source" STRING "Core Rules"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The lab (but not necessarily the living quarters of the magus) is not housed in a building at all and is completely exposed to the elements. This Flaw should be taken with the Natural Environment Virtue (although in this case it does not take any time to gain the Virtue, since the natural environment is already present). Size may be increased to any desired number. –1 General Quality, +2 Upkeep, –1 Safety, –2 Health, –3 Aesthetics."
        REFERENCES {
            "Natural Environment" -> #tHJuz4t2HS1rYadkcOIIcbZI ^"Natural Environment"
        }
    }
    #tNwo4BiD7qWTtaaKpEv6uZCR ^"Taking Over a Laboratory" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [^"Covenant"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Source" STRING "Core Rules"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Sometimes a maga finds herself in the situation of moving into a lab that was previously owned or used by someone else. If such a lab has a Refinement score of zero or less, or if the lab has a positive Refinement but was designed for transient use (as the spare labs at Durenmar are, for example), then the new owner may simply move in and begin work straight away. In this case, there is no need to change the lab’s statistics. If a lab is unique and has a positive Refinement score, however, then the new owner will find it unfamiliar and must undertake a season of rearrangement (and possibly exploration) before it can be used. This counts as a season spent to increase the Refinement, with a chance to gain the Highly Organized and Spotless Virtues or the Hidden Defect Flaw (as detailed above), except that the resulting Refinement score of the lab is equal to its old Refinement, or the new owner’s Magic Theory – 3, whichever is lower. If the new Refinement score is lower, the lab may now have more points of Virtues minus points of Flaws than is permitted. In this case, one or more Virtues are lost — the lab was sufficiently advanced or exotic that the new owner was unable to incorporate all of its improvements into her method. Finally, the storyguide should secretly make a Perception + Magic Theory roll against an Ease Factor of three times the lab’s original Refinement for the maga. If the roll fails, the Predecessor Flaw is gained, as the lab retains some foibles of the previous owner. If the roll botches, the Hidden Defect Flaw is gained in addition."
        REFERENCES {
            "Highly Organized" -> #teqkMiXWJMQ4VbmD5tZCB9Yw ^"Highly Organized"
            "Hidden Defect" -> #tSgAFrFl9SlwmM5Du4ZzcK1u ^"Hidden Defect"
            "Magic Theory" -> #t7KPhjriPvQO5FqBFYxCbWYN ^"Magic Theory"
            "Magic Theory" -> #t7KPhjriPvQO5FqBFYxCbWYN ^"Magic Theory"
            "Hidden Defect" -> #tSgAFrFl9SlwmM5Du4ZzcK1u ^"Hidden Defect"
        }
    }
    #t9taw9WAbG1UIJWmv14tpjef ^"Greater Guardian" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Laboratory Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Major" FIXED
            ^"Group" STRING "Supernatural" FIXED
            ^"Repeatable" BOOLEAN false
            ^"Source" STRING "Core Rules"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A powerful supernatural creature (Might 20 or higher), which is not the familiar of the owner, resides in the lab and acts as its protector, being well-disposed to the owner. Woe betide any who should intrude. +(creature’s Intelligence) Safety, +1 Warping, +1 Aesthetics; 3 points on appropriate Art specialization(s)."
    }
    #thkKL4ExPRs6jurKVsyllHhx ^"Greater Horde" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Laboratory Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Magnitude" STRING "Major" FIXED
            ^"Group" STRING "Supernatural" FIXED
            ^"Repeatable" BOOLEAN false
            ^"Source" STRING "Core Rules"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A large community of resident minor supernatural creatures are at the owner’s command. They are intelligent enough to serve a protective function and assist with simple lab tasks. +2 General Quality, +1 Upkeep, +(creature’s Intelligence) Safety, +2 Aesthetics; 2 points on Rego or other appropriate Art specialization(s)."
    }
    #teyuEYpx02WUrjaYLAi8rTZZ ^"Familiar" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Laboratory Virtue"
