                        "Faerie Lore" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "faerie mounds"
                        "Folk Ken" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "magi"
                        "Infernal Lore" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "curses"
                        "Latin" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "Hermetic usage"
                        "Living Language" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "storytelling"
                        "Magic Lore" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "regiones"
                        "Magic Sensitivity" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "auras"
                        "Magic Theory" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "learning spells"
                        "Order of Hermes Lore" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "history"
                        "Organization Lore: Covenant" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "personalities"
                        "Philosophiae" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "experimental philosophy"
                        "Profession: Scribe" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "copying"
                }
                ABILITIES "Abilities at Age 30:" {
                        "Area Lore" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "geography"
                        "Artes Liberales" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "astronomy"
                        "Awareness" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "determining effect"
                        "Brawl" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "Fist"
                        "Charm" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "first impressions"
                        "Etiquette" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "faeries"
                        "Faerie Lore" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "faerie mounds"
                        "Folk Ken" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "magi"
                        "Infernal Lore" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "curses"
                        "Latin" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "Hermetic usage"
                        "Living Language" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "storytelling"
                        "Magic Lore" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "regiones"
                        "Magic Sensitivity" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "auras"
                        "Magic Theory" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "learning spells"
                        "Order of Hermes Lore" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "history"
                        "Organization Lore: Covenant" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "personalities"
                        "Philosophiae" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "experimental philosophy"
                        "Profession: Scribe" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "copying"
                }
                ABILITIES "Abilities at Age 45:" {
                        "Area Lore" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "geography"
                        "Artes Liberales" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "astronomy"
                        "Awareness" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "determining effect"
                        "Brawl" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "Fist"
                        "Charm" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "first impressions"
                        "Concentration" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "academic work"
                        "Dominion Lore" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "divine creatures"
                        "Etiquette" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "faeries"
                        "Faerie Lore" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "faerie mounds"
                        "Folk Ken" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "magi"
                        "Infernal Lore" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "curses"
                        "Latin" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "Hermetic usage"
                        "Living Language" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "storytelling"
                        "Magic Lore" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "regiones"
                        "Magic Sensitivity" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "auras"
                        "Magic Theory" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "learning spells"
                        "Order of Hermes Lore" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "history"
                        "Organization Lore: Covenant" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "personalities"
                        "Philosophiae" SCORE 7 SPECIALTY "experimental philosophy"
                        "Profession: Scribe" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "copying"
                }
                PERSONALITY_TRAITS {
                        "Angry"
                        "Bitter"
                        "Resentful"
                        "Pessimistic"
                        "Resolute"
                        "Worldly-Wise"
                }
                CHOICES {
                        CHOICE [^"Broken Vessel", ^"Missing Eye", ^"Offensive to (Beings)"]
                        CHOICE [^"Covenfolk", ^"Failed Apprentice", ^"Magician", ^"Natural Philosopher", ^"Teacher"]
                        "Alternatively, a Personality Flaw representing his continued bad feelings about the events that stripped his Gift from him would be entirely appropriate in place of a physical defect."
                }
                NOTES {
                        "Age and Characteristics" "Apprentices can be taken at any age, though magi work hard to find them in their youth, when they can be molded into the image of a magus. A Failed Apprentice joining the covenant upon losing his Gift will probably be younger than 25, while one who has traveled before finding his place will be older.\n\nThe Failed Apprentice is normally intelligent, so as to take the mental rigors of a learned life, and hardy to withstand the toll of working magic, so Intelligence and Stamina should be his primary characteristics. Positive Perception or Dexterity will also benefit him, depending on what Supernatural Abilities remain."
                        "Suggested Abilities" "A Failed Apprentice would have been tutored in academic and arcane knowledge until his Gift deserted him. Beyond that, he can take and improve any Abilities that his background suggests."
                        "Personality Traits" "A Failed Apprentice may be Angry, Bitter, or Resentful over whatever took his Gift from him. The experience may have made him either Pessimistic or Resolute in the face of new challenges. But in either case, he may approach life with a new Worldly-Wise aspect."
                        "As Companion" "Grogs have a limited number of slots open for Virtues and Flaws and so have a limited range of Supernatural Abilities open to them. Companions and Mythic Companions may take more of these. They may also take Story Flaws relating to the events, perhaps Plagued by Supernatural Entity, or even Dark Secret, in addition to a Magical Air."
                }
                DESCRIPTION "I could have been like them, you know. I should have been like them! But... that was a long time ago, and where else is there for me to go?\n\nIt is the hope of every magus that the apprentice he trains embraces the magical teachings of Bonisagus, swears the Oath, and follows his master’s path into the Order of Hermes. But for some, those hopes are dashed, and the apprentice proves little more than a broken vessel to be discarded and replaced. Where should these young students go, with the truth of the supernatural world revealed to them, and no place in mundane society?\n\nRobbed of his Gift, but with knowledge of the supernatural and Bonisagus’ theories, the Failed Apprentice still has much to offer to a covenant. If taken from his parents at a very young age, life in a covenant is possibly the only life he has ever known. If he doesn’t feel he can stay with his former master, he may seek out another covenant, either one that is friendly to his own, or one that he knows would offend the magus responsible for the loss of his Gift.\n\nA Failed Apprentice may find himself busy in copying and preparing texts, assisting within the laboratory, or advising covenfolk both at home and on their journeys on supernatural matters."
                REFERENCES {
                    "Order of Hermes" -> #tARMDefConceptOrderOfHermes ^"Order of Hermes"
                    "Failed Apprentice" -> ^"Failed Apprentice"
                    "Failed Apprentice" -> ^"Failed Apprentice"
                }
            }
    "The Farrier"
    DEF {
                EXTENDS ^"Grog"
                PROPERTIES {
                    ^"Source" STRING "Grogs"
                }
                VIRTUES {
                    ^"Animal Ken"
                    ^"Craft Guild Training"
                    ^"Mythic Farrier"
                    ^"Puissant Ability" OF "Craft: Farrier"
                }
                ABILITIES "Abilities at Age 15 (Apprentice):" {
                        "Animal Handling" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "horses"
                        "Area Lore" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "local"
                        "Awareness" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "animals"
                        "Bargain" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "equine"
                        "Brawl" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "grappling"
                        "Carouse" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "stories"
                        "Craft: Farrier" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "shoes"
                        "Native Language" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "peasants"
                        "Organization Lore: Farriers’ Guild" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "regulations"
                        "Ride" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "jumping"
                }
                ABILITIES "Abilities at Age 25 (Journeyman):" {
                        "Animal Handling" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "horses"
                        "Area Lore" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "local"
                        "Awareness" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "animals"
                        "Bargain" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "equine"
                        "Brawl" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "grappling"
                        "Carouse" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "stories"
                        "Craft: Blacksmith" SCORE 3 PUISSANT 15 SPECIALTY "horseshoes"
                        "Craft: Farrier" SCORE 5 PUISSANT 15 SPECIALTY "shoes"
                        "Native Language" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "peasants"
                        "Organization Lore: Farriers’ Guild" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "regulations"
                        "Ride" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "jumping"
                        "Swim" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "diving"
                }
                ABILITIES "Abilities at Age 40 (Master):" {
                        "Animal Handling" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "horses"
                        "Area Lore" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "local"
                        "Awareness" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "animals"
                        "Bargain" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "equine"
                        "Brawl" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "grappling"
                        "Carouse" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "stories"
                        "Craft: Blacksmith" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "horseshoes"
                        "Craft: Farrier" SCORE 6 SPECIALTY "shoes"
                        "Guile" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "fraud"
                        "Native Language" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "peasants"
                        "Organization Lore: Farriers’ Guild" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "regulations"
                        "Ride" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "jumping"
                        "Swim" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "diving"
                }
                CHOICES {
                        CHOICE [^"Curse of Slander", ^"Imagined Folk Tradition Vulnerability", ^"Independent Craftsman", "Necessary", "Vulnerable to Folk Tradition"]
                        CHOICE [^"Athletic Childhood", ^"Social Childhood", ^"Craftsman", ^"Farmer", ^"Animal Trainer", ^"Covenfolk", ^"Trainer"]
                }
                NOTES {
                        "Suggested Abilities" "Suggested abilities are: Animal Handling, Craft: Farrier, Craft: Blacksmith, Bargain.\n\nThe Craftsman package should use Craft: Farrier for Craft Type A, and Animal Handling or Craft: Blacksmith for Craft B."
                        "Social Status" "Craftsman seems the logical choice, although Wanderer or Outcast is appropriate for a newcomer or a troubled individual, or Covenfolk for a long-term employee."
                        "As Companion" "Using the Farrier concept as a companion gives even more reason to play with the supernatural side of it. The increased range of Virtues possible allows Mythic Farrier to be expanded with a second form, or even replaced by the Touched by [Realm] Major Virtue in order to avoid some of the restrictions of the Minor version (City & Guild, page 71). Furthermore, Puissant (Ability), Affinities, Increased, or Great Characteristic can boost the potential Craft Totals considerably. Various Social Status Virtues from City & Guild could improve the Farrier’s place in society and his workshop, and possibly give him the benefits of assistants. But the main idea is making him a character worth playing and bringing along on adventures, instead of having him just hammer away in his shop. Investing in the Arcane Lore Virtue would make him a fine choice to bring along when investigating exotic locales for minerals — for him to use in his horseshoes — or for supernaturally aligned riding beasts."
                }
                DESCRIPTION "Some say an army marches on its stomach. But an army of horses marches very poorly indeed without proper hoof care, or if not professionally shod. An expert in this field is a prized asset in any army, caravan, or covenant. The Farrier is an important professional, needed wherever horses are in use. He is more craftsman than animal wrangler. While regular stable boys and groomsmen take care of the day-to-day tending and the hard labor of fetching water and mucking out the stables, the Farrier has more specialized skills. His primary area of expertise is caring for horses’ hooves and fitting horseshoes, as well as general equine veterinary skills. The village blacksmith might have wrought the shoe, and could shoe the horse, if need be. But the Farrier can adapt, modify, and fit it optimally. Where many horses need care, a specialized Farrier is of great value. Some people even attribute to a good Farrier supernatural abilities; this may or may not be the case.\n\nGeneral Background\n\nA wholly mundane Farrier could be the usual misfit or tragic figure, a person having lost everything or fallen to the bottom rung of society. Alternatively, he could be a person who has made enemies of nobles or been shunned by the craft guild. Such a character could easily be lured by a secure, free, and comfortable position at a well-off covenant.\n\nA supernaturally aligned Farrier could either be shunned by society in general and by the Church in particular, or be harassed or sought after by magi, hedge wizards, or supernatural beings. And as such, only a covenant with a fair Aegis of the Hearth offers any real sanctuary. Depending on the supernatural abilities of the Farrier, covenants and magi could be anything from mildly to very interested. Small, mundane enhancements of quality, or even magical abilities, are great boons to the riders of a covenant turb. And this is nothing to the advantages a Mercer House could gain for their Redcaps."
            }
    "The Jack-of-All-Trades"
    DEF {
                EXTENDS ^"Grog"
                PROPERTIES {
                    ^"Source" STRING "Grogs"
                }
                ABILITIES "Abilities at Age 22:" {
                        "Animal Handling" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "oxen"
                        "Area Lore" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "jobs"
                        "Athletics" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "climbing"
                        "Awareness" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "being watched"
                        "Brawl" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "punches"
                        "Chirurgy" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "cuts"
                        "Craft: Wrought Iron" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "nails"
                        "Folk Ken" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "employers"
                        "Guile" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "qualifications"
                        "Native Language" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "wide vocabulary"
                        "Profession: Farmer" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "plowing"
                        "Profession: Storyteller" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "bawdy tales"
                        "Single Weapon" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "axe"
                        "Stealth" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "inside"
                        "Survival" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "on the road"
                }
                ABILITIES "Abilities at Age 34:" {
